# TripSync environment variables
#
# Names and comments only — never commit real values.
# Locally, copy this file to `.dev.vars` (the file Wrangler and `next dev` read
# through the Cloudflare bindings). In production, set the same names as
# encrypted secrets on the hosting project.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Supabase Postgres
# Dashboard → your project → Connect → Connection pooling → Transaction mode
# (port 6543; the direct 5432 connection is IPv6-only and does not work from
# Render). The URI looks like:
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
# The same value goes in this file locally and in Render → Environment.
# Nothing here creates tables: the app applies drizzle/0000_init.sql on the
# first request (see /api/health).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessions (Better Auth)
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET signs session cookies. Generate one with
# `openssl rand -base64 32` and keep it server-side.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL must be the exact public origin, e.g. https://tripsync.example.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI itinerary planner (server only)
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint works. The key is read only
# inside the route handler and is never sent to the browser.
# Leave these empty to keep generation disabled: the planner reports that it is
# not configured instead of returning sample suggestions.
#
# Recommended for this project — Google AI Studio (Gemini) free tier:
#   AI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
#   AI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# Use a current model id: Gemini retires old ones (gemini-2.0-flash was shut
# down on 1 June 2026), and a retired id makes every draft fail with 502.
# Alternatives (same three variables, nothing else changes):
#   Groq        https://api.groq.com/openai/v1        llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#   OpenRouter  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1          (any model slug)
#   OpenAI      https://api.openai.com/v1             gpt-4o-mini
# AI_PROVIDER is only a label used in diagnostics.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI_PROVIDER=
AI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
AI_MODEL=
AI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email (optional)
# Invitations fall back to secure share links when this is not configured.
# Password reset reports that email is unavailable rather than pretending to
# send a message. Setting a provider also makes email verification mandatory
# for password sign-ups and sends real invitation mail.
#
# Two providers, chosen with EMAIL_PROVIDER (default: resend):
#   resend  RESEND_API_KEY  — Resend only sends from a DOMAIN you own and have
#                             verified with DNS records. Without a domain its
#                             test sender can only mail your own address.
#   brevo   BREVO_API_KEY   — Brevo only needs a verified SENDER ADDRESS (it
#                             mails a 6-digit code), so no domain is required.
#                             Free tier: 300 emails/day.
# EMAIL_FROM is the sender in both cases: `TripSync <you@example.com>`.
# Locally these go in `.dev.vars`; for the deployed site set the same names as
# environment variables on the host.
# EMAIL_API_BASE is a development-only endpoint override (https, or http for
# loopback only) used by the local capture-server tests; leave it unset in
# production so the provider's API is used.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EMAIL_PROVIDER=
RESEND_API_KEY=
BREVO_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
EMAIL_API_BASE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with Google (optional, both required together)
# Create them in Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application). Authorised redirect URI must be:
#   <origin>/api/auth/callback/google
# e.g. http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google for local work.
# While unset, the "Continue with Google" button stays hidden.
# With RESEND_API_KEY + EMAIL_FROM set, password sign-ups also require a
# verified email before the account can sign in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
